Q: How to reuse html/CSS/JavaScript in a static web site? A: <p>You can append html with the use of JS. Just add a wrapper which will contain all the cards.</p>

<p>html:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;div class="cards"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>javascript:</p>

<pre><code>const cards = document.querySelector('.cards');

function cardHtml(myData) {
    return `&lt;div class="card"&gt;&lt;p&gt;${myData}&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;`;
}

getRealtimeUpdates = function() {
    docRef.onSnapshot(function (doc) {
        if (doc &amp;&amp; doc.exists) {
            const myData = doc.data();
            cards.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', cardHtml(myData));
        }
    });
};

getRealtimeUpdates();
</code></pre>

Q: What purpose do C++23&#39;s type-identity alloc copy/move constructors serve in std::vector? A: <ul>
<li><code>other</code>'s type is actually <code>const vector&lt;T, Allocator&gt;&amp;</code> which contains <code>Allocator</code>.</li>
<li><code>alloc</code>'s type also contains <code>Allocator</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Hence you have a situation similar to <code>foo(1.0, 0)</code>. The designer of the ctor. decided, that  <code>Allocator</code> should be deduced from <code>other</code>.</p>
<p>The following example will help understand the difference between using <code>std::type_identity_t</code> and not using it (<a href="https://godbolt.org/z/53hMo8bYP" rel="nofollow noreferrer">online</a>):</p>
<pre><code>#include &lt;vector&gt;
#include &lt;memory_resource&gt;

template &lt;class T, class Allocator&gt;
struct MyVector {
    MyVector();
    MyVector(const MyVector&amp; other, const Allocator&amp; alloc);
    MyVector(MyVector&amp;&amp; other, const Allocator&amp; alloc);
};

template &lt;class T&gt; struct All1 : std::allocator&lt;T&gt; {};
template &lt;class T&gt; struct All2 : All1&lt;T&gt; {};
template &lt;class T&gt; using PMA = std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator&lt;T&gt;;

template &lt;template &lt;class, class&gt; class Vector, class A1, class A2&gt;
void Tryout(Vector&lt;int, A1&gt; v, A2 a)
{
    Vector v2(v, a);
}

int main()
{
    Tryout&lt;std::vector, All1&lt;int&gt;, All2&lt;int&gt;&gt;({}, {});
    Tryout&lt;std::vector, PMA&lt;int&gt;, std::pmr::memory_resource*&gt;({}, {});

    // error while constructing 'v2': template parameter 'Allocator' is ambiguous
    // Tryout&lt;MyVector, All1&lt;int&gt;, All2&lt;int&gt;&gt;({}, {});
    // Tryout&lt;MyVector, PMA&lt;int&gt;, std::pmr::memory_resource*&gt;({}, {});
}
</code></pre>
